    "phrases": [
      "In 1916, Germany became the first country",
      "to adopt daylight saving time",
      "nationwide, during wartime.",
      "America adopted it, repealed",
      "it despite a presidential veto, then restored it.",
      "Why?",
      "Earlier proposals and local trials existed.",
      "War accelerated adoption.",
      "In 1918, America shifted clocks to save resources.",
      "After the war, savings were disputed.",
      "Why did this trouble some farmers?",
      "Clocks shifted.",
      "The sun and dew didn't.",
      "At hearings, some complained:",
      "hired workers waited for dew to dry;",
      "stores in nearby towns closed an hour earlier.",
      "Other objections arose.",
      "In 1919, Congress repealed federal seasonal clock",
      "changes, overriding Wilson's veto.",
      "In 1942, another war restored it: clocks advanced",
      "an hour year-round.",
      "Separate legislation ended it September 30, 1945.",
      "1966 standardized scheduling with state opt-outs.",
      "Today's dates began in 2007.",
      "War didn't invent it; it accelerated its spread",
